
QuickBite Data Analyst Assessment

Project Intro

This project was done by me as part of the Data Analyst assessment.
The dataset contains information about food orders, customers, restaurants, delivery partners, areas, and customer feedback.
My main aim of this project was to clean the data,combine the tables, and find useful information from the order data using Python and Pandas.

Tools Used in this project :

* Python
* Pandas
* Excel
* VS Code

1.Data Cleaning

The dataset contained six tables.Each table had more issues that needed to be checked and cleaned before using the data for analysis.

Orders Table

* Some date and time values were stored in different formats.
* The order amount column contained currency symbols and commas.
* Payment mode and order status values had extra spaces and inconsistent text.
* Delivery time values contained text such as "mins" and "m".
* I converted the date and time values into a proper format and removed unwanted characters from the amount and delivery time columns.
* Text values were cleaned to make them consistent.
* Missing delivery time values were kept as missing instead of filling them with incorrect values.

Customers Table

* Some customer records were repeated.
* Customer names had extra spaces.
* Phone numbers contained characters such as spaces, hyphens, and the country code.
* Email values were not in a consistent format.
* I removed exact duplicate rows and cleaned the names, phone numbers, and email values.
* Phone numbers were kept as text because they are not used for calculations.

Areas Table

* Some city names were written in different ways.
* For example, short forms and full city names were used in the same column.
* I changed the city names into a common format so that the same city would not appear under different names during analysis.
* The area and zone details were retained for combining the tables.

Restaurants Table

* Cusine names had extra spaces and different letter formats.
* Some rating values needed to be checked.
* The onboard date column contained date values in different formats.
* I cleaned the cuisine names, checked the rating values, and converted the onboard dates into a proper date format.
* Missing values were not filled with random data.

Delivery Partners Table

* Some partner records were repeated.
* Vehicle names were written in different ways.
* The join date column needed to be converted into a proper date format.
* I removed exact duplicate rows and cleaned the text values.
* Phone numbers were kept as text.
* I checked the vehicle types before using them for vehicle performance analysis.

Feedback Table

* Some comments contained extra spaces and unwanted blank characters.
* The feedback date values were not in a consistent format.
* Rating values needed to be checked.
* I cleaned the comments, converted the feedback dates, and checked that the ratings were within the expected range.
* Empty comments and missing ratings were kept as missing values.

2.Combining the Tables

After cleaning the six tables, I combined them into one dataset for analysis.

The orders table was used as the main table because it contains the order details.

I used the following columns to connect the tables:

* Customer ID
* Restaurant ID
* Area ID
* Partner ID
* Order ID

The customer name was added from the customers table.

Restaurant name and cuisine were added from the restaurants table. The restaurant's area ID was then used to get the area name and city from the areas table.

Delivery partner name and vehicle type were added using the partner ID.

Customer feedback was added using the order ID.

I also created some new columns from the order date and time:

* Order Date
* Order Time
* Order Day
* Is Late

An order was marked as late when the delivery time was more than 45 minutes. If the delivery time was missing, the late status was also kept as missing.

Issues Faced While Combining

* I got a NameError because the DataFrame name was different in the cleaning script. I checked the variable names and used the correct one.
* I got a KeyError when trying to select columns that had not been created yet. I created the required columns before selecting them.
* I got an error because the os module was not imported. I added the required import.
* I faced a PermissionError while saving the Excel file because it was open. I closed the file and ran the script again.

After combining, I selected the required 19 columns and saved the final dataset.

3.Data Analysis

For the analysis, I used only the combined dataset.
I selected delivered orders for the performance calculations because cancelled orders should not be included in delivery performance.

Area Performance

The purpose of this analysis was to compare the performance of different areas.

I calculated:

* Total orders
* Total revenue
* Average delivery time
* Number of late orders
* Late delivery percentage

The results help to identify areas with higher revenue and areas where delivery time needs improvement.

Top Cuisine by Day

This analysis was done to find which cuisine received the highest number of delivered orders on each day.

I grouped the data by order day and cuisine.

Then I counted the orders for each cuisine and calculated its percentage of the total orders for that day.

Finally, I selected the cuisine with the highest order count for each day.

This helps to understand which cuisines are popular on different days.

Vehicle Performance

This analysis was used to compare delivery performance based on vehicle type.

I calculated:

* Total delivered orders
* Average delivery time
* Number of late orders
* Late delivery percentage

The results help to compare delivery times across different vehicle types.

